Fix libdeflate 1.24.0 build with gcc 16.

gcc 14 and 15 accept the `evex512`/`no-evex512` target attributes, but gcc 16
dropped them (AVX10.2 spec change), so `target("evex512")` is now rejected:

    error: attribute 'target' argument 'evex512' is unknown

libdeflate's guard `GCC_PREREQ(14, 0)` is too broad and breaks under gcc 16.
Gate the EVEX512 attribute on gcc < 16 (clang keeps working as before).

--- a/source-registry-0/libdeflate-sys-1.24.0/libdeflate/lib/x86/cpu_features.h
+++ b/source-registry-0/libdeflate-sys-1.24.0/libdeflate/lib/x86/cpu_features.h
@@ -168,4 +168,4 @@
-#if (GCC_PREREQ(14, 0) || CLANG_PREREQ(18, 0, 18000000)) \
+#if ((GCC_PREREQ(14, 0) && !GCC_PREREQ(16, 0)) || CLANG_PREREQ(18, 0, 18000000)) \
 	&& !defined(__EVEX512__) /* avoid subtracting the evex512 feature */
 #  define EVEX512	",evex512"	/* needed to override potential -mno-evex512 */
 #  define NO_EVEX512	",no-evex512"
